      "content": "I'm truly sorry you're feeling this deep disillusionment. It's painful when the things we take for granted, or believe in so strongly, suddenly vanish. Finding meaning isn't always straightforward, especially after such an immense letdown. It's normal to feel lost when everything you've built around meaning doesn't hold up. Yet, even in times of crisis, remnants of your past experiences and the people you've connected with can form a different kind of foundation for you to rebuild upon. Sometimes, meaning doesn't have to be found pre-existing; it can be created again in a new way that resonates with your current state. Is there something that, even in small ways, sustains you or sparks a sense of purpose for you now?",
